===== Hardware =====
==== Opening/closing the case ====

Note: If you do it carefully then this will NOT void your warranty as there are no parts which would be damaged

The case of the Archer C5 v4 is composed of 2 pieces:

  * Top cover (white)
  * Bottom cover (gray)

  - Remove the two screws on the bottom cover.
  - Use a thin object to release the top cover from the bottom cover

=== Putting it back together ===

  - Put the top cover back on
  - Press until it clicks back nicely to the bottom cover
  - Put back the screws


==== Serial connection ====

Serial port:  TTL voltage, 115200 bps, 8N1. 

Serial port layout is (NO hardware modification needed):
  * (1) TX
  * (2) RX
  * (3) GND
  * [4] VCC (3.3V)

//Serial connection (click to enlarge) ://\\
{{media:tplink:archerc5:c5_v4_serial.jpg?500|}}

Soldering is not needed, you can connect to the serial header as shown in the picture. Don’t forget that the TX pin of the serial port must linked to the RX pin of the router and the RX to TX! 

**Warning**: Don't connect the Vcc pin of the serial port to a TTL-to-USB adapter. This might damage the board. There's no need to connect it, communication works without Vcc.


==== Switch ====

The Archer C5 v4 uses an external Gbit switch, connected by MDIO bus. Network traffic to the CPU is passed through the internal switch of the MT7620A SoC.

MediaTek already provided a [[https://github.com/objelf/linux/commit/32326d5eb43fc183329985c6331832d9ed155491|patch]] for Linux kernel 4.14 which adds support to the RTL8367S switch. This is what is used in the current OpenWrt v18.06 versions.

An updated OpenWrt RTL8367 driver with RTL8367S chip support is available for OpenWrt since 2019 summer, however the code is still under review process as it might affect other devices negatively. This will deliver official OpenWrt support for the device, till that happen it's backported and used in my v19.07 versions.

<code>
                      |
                   (RGMII)
+----------------------------+
|         RTL8367S           |
|    switch & 5x GBit PHY    |
+----------------------------+
  0     1     2     3     4
  |     |     |     |     |
 LAN4  LAN3  LAN2  LAN1  WAN
</code>

